From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjcoggan <hjcoggan2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:19 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 04/35] cmake(ui): no X11/Wayland pkg-config on Android

src/ui required x11-xcb and wayland-client from pkg-config for every
UNIX-and-not-APPLE target. The NDK has no pkg-config and Android has neither
protocol; the Vulkan surface there comes from VK_KHR_android_surface on an
ANativeWindow. Link libandroid instead.
---
 src/ui/CMakeLists.txt | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ui/CMakeLists.txt b/src/ui/CMakeLists.txt
index 5bd3dc5..6af7a70 100644
--- a/src/ui/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/ui/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -146,7 +146,12 @@ if(REXGLUE_USE_VULKAN)
 endif()
 
 # Platform-specific dependencies
-if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+if(ANDROID)
+    # No pkg-config, X11 or Wayland in the NDK; the Android surface is a
+    # VK_KHR_android_surface on an ANativeWindow, and SDL's android video
+    # driver provides the window.
+    target_link_libraries(rexui PUBLIC android)
+elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
     find_package(PkgConfig REQUIRED)
     pkg_check_modules(X11_XCB REQUIRED x11-xcb)
     # Required, not optional: vulkan/api.h pulls in <wayland-client.h> on every
